# --- Plugin-derived data (never published) --------------------------------
# Your own preset library: factory presets, purchased or downloaded presets,
# and anything carrying absolute IR paths from your machine. Bring your own.
#
# Presets normally live outside the repo entirely, under the data root
# (${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA} when installed as a plugin — see packs/paths.py).
# These rules cover the in-repo case, which is what you get when working in a
# clone with no data root configured. Scoped to the directories presets live
# in, so an ordinary .xml elsewhere in the repo is still tracked.
samples/*.xml
packs/*/templates/

# The generated observed-value catalog. It echoes every string in your presets
# — including absolute IR file paths — so it stays local. Written under the
# data root, which is the repo itself when nothing else is configured.
packs/*/observed.json

# Notes the generate and edit skills append after a run: what was stacked, what
# the user pushed back on, and which preset it applied to. Written to the same
# data root, so in a clone it lands here — and it is the user's taste, not the
# project's, so it stays local too.
packs/*/learned-tones.md
# A persistent advisory lock is what lets two match-run databases append to the
# one pack note without overwriting each other. It contains no data, but is local
# runtime state for the same reason as the note it protects.
packs/*/.learned-tones.md.lock

# The one exception: a preset generated BY this project from an IR-free
# template, kept as a runnable example and test fixture. Must come after the
# rules above or git keeps ignoring it.
!samples/Example_Clean_PR12.xml
!samples/.gitkeep

# --- Generated output -----------------------------------------------------
out/

# --- Python ---------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# --- Local tooling / OS ---------------------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json
.env
.env.*
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# Generated by scripts/au_render.swift while measuring; never part of the repo.
*.wav

# Your own playing. A reference recording, a DI to reamp, a bounce to match
# against — these are what the matcher is pointed at, and they belong to you.
# Two of them were swept into a commit by `git add -A` before this existed.
*.m4a
*.aif
*.aiff
*.flac
*.mp3

# Leftover from the schema package dissolved in #1.
schema/

# Agent worktrees created by the Agent tool; never part of the repo.
.claude/worktrees/
